<pre class="metadata">
Title: Delegation API
Shortname: delegation
Level: None
Status: CG-DRAFT
Group: fedidcg
Repository: w3c-fedid/delegation
URL: https://w3c-fedid.github.io/delegation/
Editor: Sam Goto, w3cid 50308, Google Inc. https://google.com, goto@google.com
Abstract: This specification extends the Federated Credential Management API [[FEDCM]] so that an
    identity provider can delegate the presentation of identity assertions to the user agent. The
    identity provider acts as an <em>issuer</em> of a selectively disclosable credential bound to
    a key that the user agent generates, and the user agent acts as a <em>holder</em> that
    discloses only the claims the user agreed to share, bound to the relying party (the
    <em>verifier</em>). This way, users can sign in to relying parties without the identity
    provider learning which relying parties they sign in to.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Default Biblio Display: inline
Text Macro: RP Relying Party
Text Macro: IDP Identity Provider
</pre>

